IMPORT prelude

-- Central Provident Fund Act 1953 (Singapore) -- what I can take out of my CPF, who can reach it, and where it goes when I die.
--
-- SEAT: the member of the Fund (the employee or self-employed person whose money stands to their credit in the Fund).
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 2 "applicable person"; s 15(1) (nothing leaves the Fund without the Board's authority), s 15(2) (the two
-- grounds of withdrawal left in force), s 15(3) (the further withdrawal on each birthday), s 15(6)(a) and (c) (the retirement sum
-- and the reserved amount set aside first); s 16(1) (the medisave account ring-fenced); s 24(2) (protection from creditors and
-- bankruptcy); s 24(3A) and (3B) (moneys paid on death held on trust, outside the estate); s 25(1) (who may nominate, and how a
-- nominee receives the portion), s 25(3) (a nominee under 18 is paid through the Public Trustee) and s 25(5)(a) (marriage revokes
-- a nomination).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 1 July 2026, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CPFA1953.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 15(1A) to (1C), s 15(4) (the Board's discretion to allow more), s 15(5) beyond s 25, s 15(6A) to (7A),
-- s 15AA (the Retirement Sum Scheme) and s 16(2) and (3) beyond a comment; the charges on property and the housing and
-- investment schemes; s 25(1)(a)(iii) (periodic payments to a certified nominee) and (b) (designated shares); s 25(4) to (6AA);
-- s 25A (payment through the Public Trustee where there is no nomination) beyond naming it; Parts 3A onwards; and the machinery
-- (the Board, its officers, regulation-making, commencement). The prescribed retirement sum, the reserved amount and the classes
-- prescribed as applicable persons are set by regulations that are not deposited, so they are facts I state.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the member of the Fund, with the design defaults
-- ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. It is not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Central Provident Fund Act 1953 -- my money in the Fund, from the member's seat`

§§ `2 -- am I an applicable person`

-- s 2: "'applicable person' means -- (a) a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore; or (b) for the purposes of a provision of
-- this Act or subsidiary legislation made under this Act in which the term appears, any other person of a class prescribed by
-- regulations made under section 77(1) for the purposes of that provision".
-- The prescribed classes are not deposited, so limb (b) is a fact I state.

-- The facts of my account, as I could state them. One case is one member's account at one moment.
DECLARE `My account` HAS
    `I am a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am of a class prescribed as an applicable person for this provision`           IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 2(1A)(a): an age is attained on the corresponding birthday. Completed years, as I would say my age.
    `my age in completed years`                                                       IS A NUMBER
    -- s 15(3): the further withdrawal follows a withdrawal "on the ground that he or she has attained 55 years of age".
    `I have already withdrawn on the ground of having attained 55`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `a birthday, or the other period the Minister directs, has come round since then` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 15(1): "except with the authority of the Board" -- the Board's act, so a fact I state.
    `the Board has given its authority for the withdrawal`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    -- "the sum standing to the credit of the member in the Fund": everything in all my accounts.
    `the sum standing to my credit`                                                   IS A NUMBER
    `the sum in my medisave account`                                                  IS A NUMBER
    -- s 15(6)(c): an amount the regulations require me to reserve in my ordinary account (for example, under a property
    -- charge). Prescribed, not deposited: a fact I state, 0 if none.
    `the reserved amount in my ordinary account`                                      IS A NUMBER
    -- s 15(6)(a): "such retirement sum applicable to the member as may be prescribed". Not deposited: a fact I state.
    `the retirement sum prescribed for me`                                            IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `my account` IS A `My account`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an applicable person` IF
        `my account`'s `I am a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore`
    OR  `my account`'s `I am of a class prescribed as an applicable person for this provision`

§§ `15(2) -- on what ground may I withdraw`

-- s 15(2): "Subject to section 16, a member of the Fund is entitled to withdraw the sum standing to the credit of the member in
-- the Fund at any time after the Board is satisfied that the member -- (a) has attained the age of 55 years; or (b) is not an
-- applicable person." Paragraphs (c) to (g) are "[Deleted]" (Act 39 of 2021 and Act 36 of 2023). Two grounds remain.
DECLARE `Withdrawal ground` IS ONE OF
    `section 15(2)(b): I am not an applicable person`
    `section 15(2)(a): I have attained 55`
    `no ground under section 15(2)`

-- Where both grounds are met (a foreigner aged 60), the member may rely on either. The encoding answers with (b) because it
-- reaches more of the money (see below). That ordering is the encoder's, not the Act's.
GIVEN `my account` IS A `My account`
GIVETH A `Withdrawal ground`
DECIDE `On what ground may I withdraw` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `Am I an applicable person` `my account`
            THEN `section 15(2)(b): I am not an applicable person`
        IF `my account`'s `my age in completed years` AT LEAST 55
            THEN `section 15(2)(a): I have attained 55`
        OTHERWISE `no ground under section 15(2)`

§§ `15(3) -- the further withdrawal`

-- s 15(3): "Subject to subsection (6) and section 16, a member of the Fund who has withdrawn any money from the Fund on the
-- ground that he or she has attained 55 years of age is entitled to make a further withdrawal ... on or after each subsequent
-- anniversary of his or her date of birth or such other period as the Minister may direct."
-- It names the 55 ground only. A member who withdrew under (2)(b) is outside it.
GIVEN `my account` IS A `My account`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a further withdrawal under section 15(3)` IF
        `my account`'s `I have already withdrawn on the ground of having attained 55`
    AND `my account`'s `a birthday, or the other period the Minister directs, has come round since then`

§§ `15(6) and 16(1) -- how much I can take out`

-- s 16(1): "A member of the Fund is not entitled to withdraw any sum standing to the credit of the member in the member's medisave
-- account under section 15(2)(a) or (3)." (s 16(2) and (3) close s 15AA(1) and s 15(4) in the same way; not encoded.)
-- s 16(1) does NOT name s 15(2)(b).
--
-- s 15(6): "where a member of the Fund is entitled under subsection (2)(a) or (3), or is allowed under subsection (4), to
-- withdraw ... (a) such retirement sum applicable to the member as may be prescribed must be set aside or topped-up -- (i) by
-- the member; or (ii) from the sum standing to the member's credit in the Fund, after excluding any reserved amount standing to
-- the member's credit in his or her ordinary account; and ... (c) ... such reserved amount must be set aside or topped-up in that
-- account". s 15(6) does NOT name s 15(2)(b) either.
--
-- READING (labelled): the medisave balance, the reserved amount and the retirement sum are each kept back, so what I can take is
-- my credit less all three, and never less than nothing. A second reading is possible: the set-aside is taken from "the sum
-- standing to the member's credit" without excluding medisave, so a medisave balance might count towards the retirement sum. The
-- regulations under which the set-aside is made are not deposited; the encoding follows the first reading. Topping up "by the
-- member" (s 15(6)(a)(i)) is not modelled.
GIVEN `my account` IS A `My account`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is kept back from me on the 55 ground` IS
        `my account`'s `the sum in my medisave account`
    PLUS `my account`'s `the reserved amount in my ordinary account`
    PLUS `my account`'s `the retirement sum prescribed for me`

GIVEN `my account` IS A `My account`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much may I withdraw, once the Board authorises it` IS
    CONSIDER `On what ground may I withdraw` `my account`
    WHEN `section 15(2)(b): I am not an applicable person`
        THEN `my account`'s `the sum standing to my credit`
    WHEN `section 15(2)(a): I have attained 55`
        THEN IF   `my account`'s `the sum standing to my credit` GREATER THAN `What is kept back from me on the 55 ground` `my account`
             THEN `my account`'s `the sum standing to my credit` MINUS `What is kept back from me on the 55 ground` `my account`
             ELSE 0
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 15(1): "No sum of money standing to the credit of a member of the Fund may be withdrawn from the Fund except with the
-- authority of the Board." An entitlement is not a payment until the Board authorises it.
GIVEN `my account` IS A `My account`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May money be paid out to me now` IF
        `How much may I withdraw, once the Board authorises it` `my account` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `my account`'s `the Board has given its authority for the withdrawal`

§§ `24(2) -- can my CPF be taken for my debts`

-- s 24(2): "Despite any written or other law but subject to sections 14, 14A, 22, 24A, 27, 27B, 27C, 27D, 27DA, 27DB, 27E, 27F,
-- 27G, 27H, 27N and 57C and any regulations made under section 27Q, 57F or 77(1)", contributions and moneys standing to my
-- credit "(a) are not assignable, transferable, attached, sequestered or levied upon for or in respect of any debt or claim;
-- (b) are not subject to any set-off ...; and (c) if the member is adjudicated a bankrupt ... (i) do not pass to the Official
-- Assignee ... and (ii) are deemed not to form part of the property of the member."
-- The provisions it is subject to are not encoded; whether one of them applies is a fact I state.
GIVEN `one of the provisions section 24(2) is subject to applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my CPF money be taken for my debts or in my bankruptcy` IF
    `one of the provisions section 24(2) is subject to applies`

§§ `24(3A), 24(3B) and 25(5) -- where my CPF goes when I die`

-- s 24(3A): "all moneys paid out of the Fund on or after the death of any member of the Fund are deemed to be impressed with a
-- trust in favour of -- (a) the person or persons nominated under section 25(1) by the deceased member, if any; or (b) the person
-- or persons who are entitled to the whole or a share of the moneys payable to the Public Trustee under section 25A(1), but,
-- without affecting the operation of the Estate Duty Act 1929, are deemed not to form part of the deceased member's estate or to
-- be subject to his or her debts."
-- s 24(3B): "Where any money is payable to the spouse or former spouse of a member of the Fund under section 27B(1), (2) or (3)
-- on or after the death of the member, subsection (3A) does not apply to that money." (s 27B is not encoded.)
-- s 25(5): "Any nomination made by a member of the Fund under subsection (1) is revoked -- (a) by his or her marriage ...; or
-- (b) in such other circumstances, and in such manner, as the Board may prescribe."
--
-- So my will does not reach my CPF in either case: it goes to my nominees, or to those entitled through the Public Trustee.
DECLARE `My death facts` HAS
    `I made a nomination under section 25(1)`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `I married after making it`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was revoked in circumstances the Board has prescribed`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the money is payable to my spouse or former spouse under section 27B`  IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Destination on death` IS ONE OF
    `held on trust for my nominees, outside my estate and free of my debts`
    `held on trust for those entitled through the Public Trustee under section 25A, outside my estate and free of my debts`
    -- s 24(3B) takes this money out of s 24(3A), and s 27B is not encoded: the encoding says so rather than guess.
    `not covered by this encoding: section 24(3A) does not apply to money payable under section 27B`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `My death facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my nomination still in force` IF
        `the facts`'s `I made a nomination under section 25(1)`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `I married after making it`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `it was revoked in circumstances the Board has prescribed`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `My death facts`
GIVETH A `Destination on death`
DECIDE `Where does my CPF money go when I die` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `the money is payable to my spouse or former spouse under section 27B`
            THEN `not covered by this encoding: section 24(3A) does not apply to money payable under section 27B`
        IF `Is my nomination still in force` `the facts`
            THEN `held on trust for my nominees, outside my estate and free of my debts`
        OTHERWISE `held on trust for those entitled through the Public Trustee under section 25A, outside my estate and free of my debts`

§§ `25(1) -- may I nominate, and how my nominee receives it`

-- s 25(1): "Subject to such conditions as the Board may prescribe, any member of the Fund (being an applicable person) who is at
-- least 16 years of age may, by a memorandum executed in such manner as the Board may prescribe, nominate any person to receive in
-- his or her own right -- (a) such portion of the amount payable on the member's death out of the Fund as the memorandum
-- indicates -- (i) by the payment of that portion to that person; (ii) if, at the time the Board is satisfied that the memorandum
-- is duly executed, that person is a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore -- (A) subject to sub-paragraph (B), by the
-- transfer of that portion to that person's accounts in the Fund ...; or (B) if that portion exceeds such maximum amount as the
-- Minister may determine, by the transfer of that maximum amount to that person's accounts in the Fund ..., and by the payment
-- of the excess to that person".
-- The same member who may take everything out under s 15(2)(b) may not nominate at all.
GIVEN `my account` IS A `My account`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make a nomination` IF
        `Am I an applicable person` `my account`
    AND `my account`'s `my age in completed years` AT LEAST 16

-- How the memorandum says the portion is to reach the nominee: limb (i) or limb (ii). The manner is the member's choice in the
-- memorandum ("as the memorandum indicates"), not automatic for a citizen or permanent resident nominee.
DECLARE `My nominee` HAS
    `the portion I nominated for this person`                                          IS A NUMBER
    `my memorandum provides for transfer to the nominee's own CPF accounts`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the nominee was a citizen or permanent resident when the Board accepted the memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 25(1)(a)(ii)(B), s 25(1B): "such maximum amount as the Minister may determine". Not deposited: a fact I state.
    `the maximum amount the Minister has determined for this nominee`                 IS A NUMBER
    `the nominee's age when paid`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `the nominee is my widow`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the nominee` IS A `My nominee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the portion goes into my nominee's own CPF accounts` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the nominee`'s `my memorandum provides for transfer to the nominee's own CPF accounts` THEN 0
        IF NOT `the nominee`'s `the nominee was a citizen or permanent resident when the Board accepted the memorandum` THEN 0
        IF `the nominee`'s `the portion I nominated for this person` GREATER THAN `the nominee`'s `the maximum amount the Minister has determined for this nominee`
            THEN `the nominee`'s `the maximum amount the Minister has determined for this nominee`
        OTHERWISE `the nominee`'s `the portion I nominated for this person`

GIVEN `the nominee` IS A `My nominee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the portion is paid to my nominee in money` IS
    `the nominee`'s `the portion I nominated for this person`
        MINUS `How much of the portion goes into my nominee's own CPF accounts` `the nominee`

-- s 25(3): "any portion ... which a person nominated under subsection (1) would have received by payment to that person must be
-- paid to the Public Trustee for the benefit of that person -- (a) in any case where that person is nominated to receive that
-- portion in accordance with subsection (1)(a)(i) or (ii), if that person (not being a widow of the deceased member) is below
-- 18 years of age at the time of payment of that portion". (Limb (b), for limb (iii) nominees, is not encoded.)
GIVEN `the nominee` IS A `My nominee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my nominee's money paid to the Public Trustee instead` IF
        `How much of the portion is paid to my nominee in money` `the nominee` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the nominee`'s `the nominee's age when paid` LESS THAN 18
    AND NOT `the nominee`'s `the nominee is my widow`
